    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1999-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have that \\[ 4 - (2 - 1) = 4 - 1 = 3. \\]\n\nThen \\[ (6 \\ ? \\ 3) + 3 = 5 \\]\\[ 6 \\ ? \\ 3 = 2. \\]\n\nThe only choice that works is \\(\\div.\\)\n\nThus, A is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Simplify the part without the question mark first",
        "Find the operation that makes \\(6\\ ?\\ 3=2\\)"
      ],
